这场战争已经在全球结构中造成了许多裂痕，明显的裂痕。

143
00:11:36,639 --> 00:11:42,079
Already between the US and Europe, the divisions are sharpening.
美国与欧洲之间的分歧已经日益尖锐。

144
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:47,560
Because American interests and European interests don't coincide.
因为美国的利益和欧洲的利益并不一致。

145
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:52,720
The Europeans are very dependent on Middle Eastern oil and gas.
欧洲非常依赖中东的石油和天然气。

146
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:57,440
They've already cut themselves off from Russian energy sources.
他们已经切断了与俄罗斯能源来源的联系。

147
00:11:57,440 --> 00:12:01,759
And they said, well, why are we being dragged into this?
他们说，我们为什么要被卷入其中？

148
00:12:01,759 --> 00:12:04,160
And they're reluctant to get involved in the Homo Strait.
他们不愿卷入霍尔木兹海峡的事务。

149
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:08,960
I mean, they have to see certain things because of the alliance with America.
我的意思是，由于与美国的联盟关系，他们必须关注某些事情。

150
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:12,080
But they don't really want to get too deeply involved.
但他们并不想过度深入参与。

151
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:19,000
Then in the Middle East, if you look at the Gulf states, the bases have been destroyed.
然后在中东，如果你看看海湾国家，基地已经被摧毁了。

152
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,879
The US bases have been destroyed by Iran.
美国的基地被伊朗摧毁了。

153
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:28,759
When oil is over, firstly, would the US want to rebuild those bases and maybe have them destroyed again in the future?
当石油时代结束后，首先，美国会想要重建那些基地吗？也许未来它们会再次被摧毁？

154
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:30,840
They cost a lot of money.
它们花费了大量资金。

155
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:35,800
And if you are a Gulf state, do you really want those bases to be rebuilt
如果你是一个海湾国家，你真的希望那些基地被重建吗？

156
00:12:35,799 --> 00:12:40,759
and be again sucked into a war, not of your making?
并再次被卷入一场并非由你引发的战争？

157
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:45,639
So the basing arrangements were changed.
因此，基地部署安排已经改变。

158
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:48,799
Everybody is recalculating.
每个人都在重新计算。

159
00:12:48,799 --> 00:12:53,439
So the cracks are there.
所以裂痕就在那里。

160
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,939
They were widened.
它们被扩大了。

161
00:12:54,759 --> 00:12:58,199
How they were widened when oil is over, we'll see.
石油时代结束后，它们会如何拓宽，我们拭目以待。

162
00:12:58,199 --> 00:13:00,439
But no position is static.
但没有任何立场是静止不变的。

163
00:13:00,439 --> 00:13:03,359
Everybody has to recalculate.
每个人都必须重新计算。

164
00:13:03,399 --> 00:13:06,480
And China has to recalculate.
中国也必须重新计算。

165
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:11,639
Finally, what is the one thing that you personally follow the closest
最后，就局势发展而言，您个人最密切关注的是什么？

166
00:13:11,639 --> 00:13:14,720
in terms of the development of the situation?
就局势发展而言，您个人最密切关注的是什么？

167
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,960
I'm very worried about AI.
我非常担心人工智能。

168
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:23,759
I mean, here we talk about the positive uses of AI and how it can improve human lives.
我是说，我们在这里谈论人工智能的积极用途，以及它如何改善人类生活。

169
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:29,120
I mean, if you can't walk, if you have a back problem with AI,
我是说，如果你无法行走，如果你有背部问题，借助人工智能，

170
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:33,240
you can strap on certain exoskeletons and your life is really improved.
你可以穿上某些外骨骼，你的生活真的会得到改善。

171
00:13:34,039 --> 00:13:36,680
It can help construction.
它可以帮助建筑。

172
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,039
It can help maintenance.
它可以帮助维护。

173
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,600
It can help learning.
它可以帮助学习。

174
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,519
It's wonderful.
这太棒了。

175
00:13:42,519 --> 00:13:50,600
But AI is also being used today for drone warfare and for decapitation.
但如今，人工智能也被用于无人机战争和斩首行动。

176
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:56,200
And you can be sure that the most advanced AI today is being used
你可以确信，当今最先进的人工智能正被用于

177
00:13:56,200 --> 00:14:01,560
for to kill, to wound, to damage, to intimidate.
杀戮、致残、破坏和恐吓。

178
00:14:01,559 --> 00:14:03,679
And to spread misinformation, probably.
以及传播错误信息，大概如此。

179
00:14:03,679 --> 00:14:05,359
And to spread information.
以及传播信息。

180
00:14:05,359 --> 00:14:07,719
We don't quite know how to believe nowadays.
如今我们不太知道该相信什么。

181
00:14:07,719 --> 00:14:09,759
We see something.
我们看到了某些东西。

182
00:14:09,759 --> 00:14:11,259
It looks real.
它看起来很真实。

183
00:14:10,479 --> 00:14:11,979
It may not be real.
但它可能并不真实。

184
00:14:11,359 --> 00:14:12,859
We hear words.
我们听到了话语。

185
00:14:12,439 --> 00:14:14,279
They may not be real.
它们可能并不真实。

186
00:14:14,279 --> 00:14:15,959
What do we believe?
我们该相信什么？

187
00:14:15,959 --> 00:14:22,719
So we are entering a period where a new technology arises.
所以，我们正进入一个新技术兴起的时期。

188
00:14:22,719 --> 00:14:24,239
It can do good.
它能带来善。

189
00:14:24,239 --> 00:14:27,079
It can do immense evil.
它也能造成巨大的恶。

190
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:33,440
And our moral sense, our values have not caught up.
而我们的道德观念、价值观尚未跟上。

191
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:37,440
I mean, you take decapitation.
我是说，你想想斩首行动。

192
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:40,720
Is there no limit to this?
这难道没有底线吗？

193
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:48,040
And if you, and today with AI, it's easier and easier because everybody can be tracked.
而且如今有了人工智能，这变得愈发容易，因为每个人都能被追踪。

194
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,240
And the weapons are getting smaller and smaller.
武器正变得越来越小。

195
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,740
They can go through tunnels.
它们能穿过隧道。

196
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:56,320
They can come through an open window.
它们能穿过敞开的窗户。

197
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:58,640
But I can do it to you.
但我可以对你这么做。

198
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:00,879
You can do it to me.
你也可以对我这么做。

199
00:15:00,879 --> 00:15:03,920
Are we savages?
我们是野蛮人吗？

200
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:10,800
If you are human beings and civilization is built on cooperation and win-win, how do you achieve it?
如果你们是文明人，而文明建立在合作与双赢之上，你们该如何实现这一点？

201
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:16,920
So there is a fundamental moral challenge
因此，这项新技术的到来带来了根本性的道德挑战。

202
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:20,120
to the arrival of this new technology.
这项新技术的到来带来了根本性的道德挑战。

203
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,640
Thank you so much, George Yeo, former Foreign Minister of Singapore.
非常感谢新加坡前外长杨荣文。

204
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,240
Thank you.
谢谢。

205
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:32,320
George Yeo, former Foreign Minister of Singapore.
新加坡前外长杨荣文。

206
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:37,800
In a world of growing trade uncertainty, where can we find certainty?
在贸易不确定性日益加剧的世界里，我们能在哪里找到确定性？

207
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:39,320
Stay tuned.
请继续收看。

208
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:46,920
Making sense of the overwhelming wave of information means cutting through the noise to shine a light
理清信息洪流意味着穿透噪音，照亮

209
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:49,320
on the heart of the story.
故事的核心。

210
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:56,320
And the world of the world of the world of the world to shine a light on the heart of the story.
穿透噪音，照亮故事的核心。

211
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:59,320
And making room for new perspectives.
并为新的视角腾出空间。

212
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:05,320
True understanding means the ability to see events for more than one side.
真正的理解意味着能够看到事件的多面性。

213
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,320
I'm Lee Sheen, and this is The Point.
我是李欣，这里是《锐评》。

214
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:18,320
As trade protectionism continues to rise, can China-UK trade offer a ray of light in uncertain times?
随着贸易保护主义持续抬头，中英贸易能否在不确定时期带来一丝光明？

215
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:25,320
In 2025, bilateral trade volumes surpassed 100 billion US dollars, signaling a rebound
2025年，双边贸易额突破1000亿美元，标志着

216
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,320
in this relationship.
这一关系的回暖。

217
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:33,320
That same year, high-level economic talks between the two sides resumed after a six-year pause.
同年，双方高层经济对话在暂停六年后恢复。

218
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:41,320
Here at the Boa Forum for Asia, I sit down with Peter Burnett, CEO of China-Britain Business Council.
在博鳌亚洲论坛，我与中英商会首席执行官彼得·伯内特进行对话。

219
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:46,320
What brings him here, and what is the state of China-UK trade relationship?
他为何而来，中英贸易关系现状如何？

220
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:49,320
Here is our conversation.
以下是我们的对话。

221
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:58,320
Mr. Burnett, welcome to The Point.
伯内特先生，欢迎来到《锐评》。

222
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,320
Thank you very much for sitting down with us.
非常感谢您接受我们的访谈。

223
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:04,320
So, where are we in terms of China-UK trade relationship?
那么，目前中英贸易关系处于什么状况？

224
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:09,320
We always focus more on the trading goods, but there are also the trading services,
我们通常更关注货物贸易，但服务贸易同样重要，

225
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:11,320
which is very important for UK as well.
这对英国来说也至关重要。

226
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:13,320
So, help us understand the big picture, please.
所以，请帮我们理清一下整体情况。

227
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,820
Yes, of course.
是的，当然。

228
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:17,319
Well, we're in a much better position than we were 18 months ago.
嗯，我们的处境比18个月前要好得多。

229
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:25,319
I mean, businesses have continued to do what they always do, which is to trade with each other, to sell goods,
我的意思是，企业一直在做它们一贯做的事，那就是彼此开展贸易，销售商品，

230
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:29,319
to find the right product, the right price, the right customers.
寻找合适的产品、合适的价格和合适的客户。

231
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:33,319
And that's been going on, you know, even through the eight years
而且这种情况一直持续着，你知道，甚至贯穿了那八年

232
00:17:33,319 --> 00:17:38,319
where there was no Prime Minister visit and no interaction between Chinese leaders and the British leaders.
那八年里，英国首相没有访华，中英两国领导人之间也没有任何互动。

233
00:17:38,319 --> 00:17:42,319
But of course, it's picked up enormously since the Prime Minister's visit,
但当然，自从首相访华以来，这种情况有了巨大的改善，

234
00:17:42,319 --> 00:17:49,319
and actually before that, which was January of this year, and before that, 18 months previously,
实际上在那之前，也就是今年一月，再往前推十八个月，

235
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:55,319
when Keer Starmer, Prime Minister of the United Kingdom and Xi Jinping did a phone call together,
当时英国首相基尔·斯塔默与中国国家主席习近平进行了一次通话，

236
00:17:55,319 --> 00:18:01,319
and they recognized that they were going to rebuild the relationship at a G to G level.
他们意识到将在政府间层面重建关系。

237
00:18:01,319 --> 00:18:03,319
And that matters for businesses.
这对企业至关重要。

238
00:18:03,319 --> 00:18:08,319
If you've got a strong G to G relationship, then businesses feel much more confident
如果政府间关系稳固，企业就会对

239
00:18:08,319 --> 00:18:11,319
about where they are investing and how they're doing business.
其投资方向和业务开展方式感到更加有信心。

240
00:18:11,319 --> 00:18:16,319
So I'll ask you a second question, which is the relationship between services and trade.
所以我想问你第二个问题，即服务业与贸易之间的关系。

241
00:18:16,319 --> 00:18:21,319
So trade is definitely growing and very positive.
因此，贸易确实在增长，且势头非常积极。

242
00:18:21,319 --> 00:18:28,319
The United Kingdom, along with many other parts of the world, has a trade deficit with China.
英国与世界许多其他地区一样，对华存在贸易逆差。

243
00:18:28,319 --> 00:18:32,319
So China has a surplus in trading goods with the United Kingdom.
因此，中国在对英商品贸易中拥有顺差。

244
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:37,319
But we have a trade surplus in services with China.
但我们在对华服务贸易中拥有顺差。

245
00:18:38,319 --> 00:18:41,319
And that is very good for us.
这对我们来说非常好。

246
00:18:41,319 --> 00:18:49,319
And it's very good that China, out of the 15th Five Year Plan, has identified services as a growth area for the economy.
而且，中国将服务业确定为经济增长领域，这一点非常好，这是出自“十五五”规划的。

247
00:18:49,319 --> 00:18:53,319
And there is now a feasibility being undertaken by both the Chinese government
目前，中国政府

248
00:18:53,319 --> 00:18:58,319
and the British government to look at a free trade agreement in services.
和英国政府正在进行一项可行性研究，以探讨在服务贸易方面达成自由贸易协定。

249
00:18:58,319 --> 00:19:05,319
If that happened, it would be the first bilateral between China and another sovereign state.
如果实现这一点，那将是首个中国与其他主权国家之间的双边协定。

250
00:19:05,319 --> 00:19:10,319
The United Kingdom economic output is about 80% in services.
英国的经济产出中，服务业占比约为80%。

251
00:19:10,319 --> 00:19:13,319
So it's a very, very important part of what we do.
因此，这是我们工作中非常、非常重要的一部分。

252
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:16,319
And it's very clear that China is moving up the value chain.
很明显，中国正在向价值链上游攀升。

253
00:19:16,319 --> 00:19:20,319
So it's no longer producing cheap goods cheaply.
它不再仅仅以低成本生产廉价商品。

254
00:19:20,319 --> 00:19:22,319
It's moved on from that 20, 30 years ago.
它已经超越了二三十年前那种模式。

255
00:19:22,319 --> 00:19:29,319
And it's now moving up the value chain, both in terms of technology, but also now in terms of services as well.
现在，它正在向价值链上游攀升，不仅在技术方面，也在服务领域。

256
00:19:29,319 --> 00:19:30,819
And that's where it should be.
它应该处于这个位置。

257
00:19:30,319 --> 00:19:34,319
That's where a confident, prosperous nation should be moving.
一个自信、繁荣的国家应该向这个方向迈进。

258
00:19:34,319 --> 00:19:37,319
And the United Kingdom can be part of that.
英国可以成为其中的一部分。

259
00:19:37,319 --> 00:19:39,319
So it's a good moment.
所以，这是一个很好的时机。

260
00:19:39,319 --> 00:19:46,319
So I have some numbers, for instance, in terms of trade in services, because I think that's not talked about enough,
因此，我有一些数据，例如在服务贸易方面，因为我认为这方面讨论得还不够多，

261
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:52,319
although the relative scale is still smaller compared to the trading goods.
尽管与货物贸易相比，其相对规模仍然较小。

262
00:19:52,319 --> 00:19:55,319
But the growth rate is actually very fast.
但增长率实际上非常快。

263
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:59,319
It's almost double, if I'm correct.
如果我没记错的话，几乎翻了一番。

264
00:19:59,319 --> 00:20:07,319
And China is exporting about one third of what the UK is exporting almost three times in terms of services.
在服务业方面，中国的出口额大约是英国的三倍，而英国仅出口其总量的三分之一。

265
00:20:07,319 --> 00:20:09,319
Correct. That is correct.
没错，确实如此。

266
00:20:09,319 --> 00:20:14,319
Yeah. What does that mean for UK businesses?
是的。这对英国企业意味着什么？

267
00:20:14,319 --> 00:20:17,319
What means we need to do more?
这意味着我们需要做得更多吗？

268
00:20:17,319 --> 00:20:19,319
This is a great opportunity.
这是一个绝佳的机会。

269
00:20:19,319 --> 00:20:21,319
And China is opening up in services.
而且中国正在开放服务业。

270
00:20:21,319 --> 00:20:24,319
As I say, this feasibility study is taking place.
正如我所说，这项可行性研究正在进行中。

271
00:20:24,319 --> 00:20:28,319
I very much hope that we can conclude a free trade agreement in services.
我非常希望我们能达成一项服务业自由贸易协定。

272
00:20:28,319 --> 00:20:34,319
And what services include, if you think about where the United Kingdom is strong.
至于服务业包括哪些内容，你可以想想英国的优势领域。

273
00:20:34,319 --> 00:20:36,319
So it's financial services.
所以是金融服务。

274
00:20:36,319 --> 00:20:41,319
Clearly the city of London, very well known as a global financial centre.
显然，伦敦作为全球金融中心而闻名。

275
00:20:41,319 --> 00:20:47,319
But it's also legal services, accounting services, consulting services,
但还包括法律服务、会计服务、咨询服务，

276
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:50,319
architectural services, engineering services.
建筑服务、工程服务。

277
00:20:50,319 --> 00:20:57,319
So all of those intangible services that don't require you to move a physical asset across the border.
所以所有这些不需要将实体资产跨越边境移动的无形服务。

278
00:20:57,319 --> 00:21:01,319
But it also includes the creative industries.
但它还包括创意产业。

279
00:21:01,319 --> 00:21:07,319
So football, the Premier League will tell you that it has 300 million customers in China.
所以足球，英超联赛会告诉你它在中国有3亿客户。

280
00:21:07,319 --> 00:21:10,319
It was interesting that on the Prime Minister's visit,
有趣的是，在首相访问期间，

281
00:21:10,319 --> 00:21:16,319
the heads of the associations for table tennis and snooker travelled with him.
乒乓球和斯诺克协会的负责人也随他同行。

282
00:21:16,319 --> 00:21:18,319
I'm a fan of snooker right now.
我现在是斯诺克的粉丝。

283
00:21:18,319 --> 00:21:19,819
There you go.
就是这样。

284
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:24,319
So well, that's good to hear because snooker is a UK, is a British invention, table tennis,
嗯，这听起来不错，因为斯诺克是英国的发明，乒乓球，

285
00:21:24,319 --> 00:21:31,319
the headquarters of the rule setting body is in the United Kingdom as is badminton.
制定规则的机构总部也在英国，羽毛球也是如此。

286
00:21:31,319 --> 00:21:32,819
So there are all these...
所以所有这些……

287
00:21:32,319 --> 00:21:35,319
I'm surprised it's not in China, the table tennis.
我惊讶的是乒乓球不在中国。

288
00:21:35,319 --> 00:21:40,319
Precisely, right, because the world champion is Chinese, the world champion in snooker is Chinese.
没错，因为世界冠军是中国人，斯诺克的世界冠军也是中国人。

289
00:21:40,319 --> 00:21:41,819
But guess what?
但猜猜怎么着？

290
00:21:41,319 --> 00:21:42,819
There's the potential.
这里有潜力。

291
00:21:42,319 --> 00:21:43,819
There is the potential.
确实有潜力。

292
00:21:43,319 --> 00:21:45,319
There is absolutely the potential.
绝对有潜力。

293
00:21:45,319 --> 00:21:53,319
So the more that we can export that capability into China and grow it across sports and creative industries,
因此，如果我们能将这些能力更多地输出到中国，并在体育和创意产业中推广，

294
00:21:53,319 --> 00:21:55,319
I think it's very, very interesting.
我觉得这非常、非常有趣。

295
00:21:55,319 --> 00:21:59,319
And China is, as I was saying earlier, China is at a stage in its development
正如我刚才所说，中国正处于其发展的一个阶段，

296
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:06,319
where people can afford to spend more time watching snooker, going to football matches.
人们有能力花更多时间观看斯诺克，去现场看足球比赛。

297
00:22:06,319 --> 00:22:11,319
They're going to enjoy and be entertained by all of these things.
他们会享受并从中获得所有这些事物的娱乐。

298
00:22:11,319 --> 00:22:18,319
And then beyond that, films, James Bond films, Tourism, study,
除此之外，还有电影，比如詹姆斯·邦德电影，旅游业，留学，

299
00:22:18,319 --> 00:22:21,319
Tourism, study, universities, all of those things.
旅游业，留学，大学，所有这些事物。

300
00:22:21,319 --> 00:22:25,319
These are intangibles that have great potential, I think, in China.
我认为，这些无形资产在中国具有巨大的潜力。

301
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:32,319
So this is where I very much hope that we, we're a private sector organisation, the China-Britain Business Council,
所以，这正是我非常希望我们——作为一家私营部门机构，中英商会——

302
00:22:32,319 --> 00:22:37,319
so we want to very focus very much on these areas together with both governments
能够与双方政府紧密合作，非常聚焦于这些领域，

303
00:22:37,319 --> 00:22:45,319
and bring our members along and explain to them what the opportunities are and where those opportunities are as well.
并带领我们的会员，向他们解释机遇所在以及机遇的具体位置。

304
00:22:45,319 --> 00:22:50,319
I want to focus a little bit on trading goods, because it's also growing by over 5%.
我想稍微聚焦一下货物贸易，因为它的年增长率也超过了5%。

305
00:22:50,319 --> 00:22:58,319
On annual basis, and there, increasing amount of higher-end Chinese-made goods are coming into the UK.
从年度来看，越来越多的中国高端制造产品正进入英国市场。

306
00:22:58,319 --> 00:23:03,319
And the UK, of course, is also exporting to China, but the scale is smaller.
当然，英国也在向中国出口，但规模较小。

307
00:23:03,319 --> 00:23:09,319
And interestingly, new energy vehicles is growing very fast.
有趣的是，新能源汽车正在快速增长。

308
00:23:09,319 --> 00:23:15,319
300,000 units, if I'm correct, for the last year.
如果我没记错的话，去年的销量达到了30万辆。

309
00:23:15,319 --> 00:23:20,319
What does it mean for the UK consumers, for the UK economy,
这对英国消费者、对英国经济意味着什么，

310
00:23:20,319 --> 00:23:28,319
that there is this growing imports from China in terms of good, good for jobs, good for consumers potentially?
即中国商品进口的增长，这对就业和消费者来说可能是好事？

311
00:23:28,319 --> 00:23:30,319
At the moment, it's good for consumers,
目前，这对消费者是好事，

312
00:23:30,319 --> 00:23:36,319
but we need to turn it into something which is good for jobs and economic growth.
但我们需要将其转化为有利于就业和经济增长的成果。

313
00:23:36,319 --> 00:23:38,319
So you're absolutely right.
你说得完全正确。

314
00:23:38,319 --> 00:23:42,319
The growth in EV purchases in the United Kingdom,
英国电动汽车购买量的增长，

315
00:23:42,319 --> 00:23:47,319
particularly of Chinese EVs, has grown very, very rapidly in 2025.
特别是中国电动汽车，在2025年增长得非常、非常快。

316
00:23:47,319 --> 00:23:54,319
One of the reasons for that is that the United Kingdom has no tariffs, zero tariffs on EVs.
原因之一是英国对电动汽车没有关税，即零关税。

317
00:23:54,319 --> 00:24:02,319
There are tariffs on cars, but zero additional tariffs on EVs, unlike many other jurisdictions around the world.
虽然对汽车有关税，但对电动汽车没有额外关税，这与世界上许多其他司法管辖区不同。

318
00:24:02,319 --> 00:24:08,319
And so, of course, the United Kingdom has been a destination for a lot of EV exporters, Chinese EV exporters.
因此，当然，英国已成为许多电动汽车出口商，特别是中国电动汽车出口商的目的地。

319
00:24:08,319 --> 00:24:14,319
And the comparative advantage that China has, I'm a big believer in the theory of comparative advantage,
中国拥有的比较优势，我是比较优势理论的坚定支持者，

320
00:24:14,319 --> 00:24:18,319
as proposed by the British economist David Ricciardo,
该理论由英国经济学家大卫·李嘉图提出，

321
00:24:18,319 --> 00:24:24,319
the comparative advantage that China has is cost and technology.
中国的比较优势在于成本和技术。

322
00:24:24,319 --> 00:24:28,319
It's got two comparative advantages, costs, so it produces much more cheaply,
它拥有两大比较优势，一是成本，因此生产成本更低，

323
00:24:28,319 --> 00:24:34,319
and it's also got this great technological understanding of batteries and of charging.
二是对电池和充电技术有着深刻的理解。

324
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:39,319
You can now charge a BYD in nine minutes, I understand.
我听说现在给比亚迪充电只需九分钟。

325
00:24:39,319 --> 00:24:47,319
But if it wants to continue to develop, and I'm not talking about BYD, I'm talking about the industry as a whole,
但如果它想要持续发展，我指的不是比亚迪，而是整个行业，

326
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:51,319
if the industry wants to develop further in the United Kingdom,
如果该行业希望在英国进一步发展，

327
00:24:51,319 --> 00:24:55,319
it has to bring the technology comparative advantage to that country.
它就必须将技术比较优势带到那个国家。

328
00:24:55,319 --> 00:24:56,819
Which means?
这意味着什么？

329
00:24:56,319 --> 00:25:02,319
Because it means it needs to invest in production assembly in the UK.
因为这意味着它需要在英国投资生产组装。

330
00:25:02,319 --> 00:25:07,319
In the same way as the Japanese did, for example, going back 20, 25 years
就像日本人在20、25年前那样，

331
00:25:07,319 --> 00:25:11,319
when they built huge car plants in Nissan.
当时日产建立了巨大的汽车工厂。

332
00:25:11,319 --> 00:25:14,319
The UK is a big car market, right?
英国是一个庞大的汽车市场，对吧？

333
00:25:14,319 --> 00:25:23,319
Germany is also a big car market, but it's also got a very big home vehicle production capability.
德国也是一个庞大的汽车市场，但它同时也拥有非常强大的本土汽车生产能力。

334
00:25:23,319 --> 00:25:27,319
The UK has big vehicle production capabilities,
英国拥有庞大的汽车生产能力，

335
00:25:27,319 --> 00:25:32,319
but it's owned by the Japanese, by the Germans, and to some extent by the Chinese.
但这些产能由日本人、德国人以及在一定程度上由中国人拥有。

336
00:25:32,319 --> 00:25:35,319
And we want to see more of that investment.
我们希望看到更多的此类投资。

337
00:25:35,319 --> 00:25:39,319
That will provide jobs, it will provide growth,
这将提供就业机会，促进增长，

338
00:25:39,319 --> 00:25:49,319
and it will deal with the potential criticism that what we are seeing is just exporting capacity.
并回应那种认为我们看到的只是产能出口的潜在批评。

339
00:25:49,319 --> 00:25:50,819
Right.
没错。

340
00:25:50,319 --> 00:25:53,319
I want to ask you exactly that.
我想向你提出完全相同的问题。

341
00:25:53,319 --> 00:25:58,319
What keeps you awake at night as a promoter of China-UK trade?
作为中英贸易的推动者，是什么让您夜不能寐？

342
00:25:58,319 --> 00:26:04,319
You just said consumers potentially benefiting, but jobs, which is a very important factor.
您刚才说消费者可能会受益，但就业也是一个非常重要的因素。

343
00:26:04,319 --> 00:26:06,319
So how do you balance that?
那么您如何平衡这两者？

344
00:26:06,319 --> 00:26:12,319
So what is the one biggest question you're focusing on in promoting this trade relationship?
所以在促进这一贸易关系时，您最关注的一个大问题是什么？

345
00:26:12,319 --> 00:26:14,319
I sleep very well, actually.
其实我睡得非常好。

346
00:26:14,319 --> 00:26:16,319
So things are going well?
所以一切进展顺利？

347
00:26:16,319 --> 00:26:21,319
That may not be a reflection of the state of affairs, it just may be my DNA or my makeup.
这可能并不反映实际情况，也许只是我的天性或性格使然。

348
00:26:21,319 --> 00:26:23,319
Because you're optimistic or...?
因为您很乐观，还是……？

349
00:26:23,319 --> 00:26:25,319
I have to be optimistic, yes.
我必须保持乐观，是的。

350
00:26:25,319 --> 00:26:28,319
I have to be optimistic about two-way trade between both countries.
我必须对两国之间的双向贸易保持乐观。

351
00:26:28,319 --> 00:26:35,319
I don't think there's any other state of mind that you can have when you're in this field.
我认为在这个领域，你不可能拥有其他心态。

352
00:26:35,319 --> 00:26:43,319
But what we want to see is where there are tariffs reduced,
但我们希望看到关税降低的地方，

353
00:26:43,319 --> 00:26:50,319
it was very good to see the tariff on whiskey come down from 10% to 5% as a result of the Prime Minister visit.
很高兴看到威士忌关税因首相的访问而从10%降至5%。

354
00:26:50,319 --> 00:26:55,319
But we want to see smoother access, in particular, into the China market.
但我们希望看到更顺畅的市场准入，特别是进入中国市场。

355
00:26:55,319 --> 00:27:02,319
So China now has this initiative, big market for all, export to China.
所以中国现在有这个倡议，面向所有国家的大市场，出口到中国。

356
00:27:02,319 --> 00:27:06,319
The UK is a pilot country inside that initiative.
英国是该倡议内的试点国家。

357
00:27:06,319 --> 00:27:19,319
And what we want to see are some measures, some measures which allow exports to be more freely and more easily exported and crossed the border into China.
我们希望看到一些措施，一些能让出口更自由、更容易跨越边境进入中国的措施。

358
00:27:19,319 --> 00:27:27,319
So it's more than a slogan, we actually see, for example, some further tariff reductions where that's needed.
所以这不仅仅是一句口号，我们实际上看到，例如，在需要的地方进一步降低关税。

359
00:27:27,319 --> 00:27:38,319
And we see a faster approval of products, including foodstuffs and animal feeds and things like that and agricultural products.
我们看到产品审批速度加快，包括食品、动物饲料以及农产品等。

360
00:27:38,319 --> 00:27:45,319
And maybe a facility through e-commerce which allows those goods to quickly get into the marketplace.
也许通过电子商务设施，让这些商品能迅速进入市场。

361
00:27:45,319 --> 00:27:54,319
And fortunately, it would be very good to see a direct connection between exporters in the UK and buyers in China.
幸运的是，看到英国出口商与中国买家建立直接联系将是非常好的事情。

362
00:27:54,319 --> 00:28:04,319
And we could rebalance some of that disproportionate trade number so that we didn't have such a big trade deficit.
我们可以重新平衡那些失衡的贸易数据，从而避免如此巨大的贸易逆差。

363
00:28:04,319 --> 00:28:14,319
I see. Well, time very limited, but I got the points and I'm happy that you're working hard but you're not losing any sleep over it.
我明白了。时间非常有限，但我明白了你的观点，我很高兴你工作很努力，但并没有为此寝食难安。

364
00:28:14,319 --> 00:28:19,319
There's no point in losing it because I think the overall goal is common, is shared.
为此焦虑没有意义，因为我认为总体目标是共同的，是共享的。

365
00:28:19,319 --> 00:28:23,319
It's absolutely common. It's growth, it's job, it's prosperity.
这绝对是共同的。它是增长，是就业，是繁荣。

366
00:28:23,319 --> 00:28:29,319
The theme of the Boal Forum is shaping a shared future and I think the most important word there is shared.
博鳌论坛的主题是塑造共同的未来，我认为其中最重要的词是“共同”。

367
00:28:29,319 --> 00:28:32,319
We've got to work together. We've got to be cooperative.
我们必须携手合作。我们必须保持协作。

368
00:28:32,319 --> 00:28:35,319
Absolutely. I wish you all the very best.
绝对如此。祝你们一切顺利。

369
00:28:35,319 --> 00:28:40,319
Peter Burnett, CEO of China-Britain Business Council, CBBC. Thank you.
彼得·伯内特，中英商会（CBBC）首席执行官。谢谢你。

370
00:28:40,319 --> 00:28:42,319
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

371
00:28:42,319 --> 00:28:53,319
Peter Burnett, CEO of China-Britain Business Council.
彼得·伯内特，中英商会首席执行官。

372
00:28:53,319 --> 00:29:00,319
With that, we'll come to the end of this special edition of The Point with me, Lee Xin, coming to you from Boal in Southern China.
至此，由我李欣在中国南方博鳌为您带来的《锐评》特别节目就到此结束了。

373
00:29:00,319 --> 00:29:06,319
As always, you can follow me on Facebook and X using the handle Lee Xin in Beijing on YouTube as well.
一如既往，您可以在 Facebook 和 X 上关注我的账号 Lee Xin in Beijing，也可以在 YouTube 上关注。

374
00:29:06,319 --> 00:29:10,319
On behalf of the whole team, thank you for watching. You've got the point.
代表整个团队，感谢收看。您已抓住要点。

375
00:29:12,319 --> 00:29:14,319
Thank you.
谢谢。

376
00:29:42,319 --> 00:29:44,319
Thank you.
谢谢。
